title ALES205 — Lotus's stereo reverberant tone shelf, the reverb's two-band EQ per ear
prompt recur loop — continue the Lotus/ALES ladder Lindy-first crux-first, each finished rung its own signed round pushed to origin and xykj61, stop at the custody gates
think ALES204 gave the mono reverb its two-band shelving EQ; the ladder always closes the mono/stereo pair before opening a fresh axis, so the thin twin is stereo_reverb_shelf — the same shelf over both channels of a StereoClip, one shared bass/treble/split, the image held. Mirrored ALES199 (stereo_reverb_tone) exactly, swapping tone.low_pass per ear for shelf.shelf per ear, and using the shelf.precheck ALES204 added for the atomicity crux.
think Reverberate the master wet through ALES191 stereo_reverb_preset unchanged; precheck the shelf setting (shelf.precheck) BEFORE the wet is written so a bad shelf leaves both channels dry and balanced; then shelve each channel with no cross-channel read so the image is held. StereoReverbShelfError = stereo_reverb_preset.StereoReverbPresetError || shelf.ShelfError.
obs Witness GREEN on the first metal pass — no RED to book. Seven laws on a 1024-sample bench with two distinct impulses: the identity edge on both channels, each channel equals its composition (stereo_reverb_preset then shelf.shelf) byte for byte and differs from its wet, the treble cut darkens per ear (roughness strictly reduced), the bass boost lifts per ear (energy strictly grown — the colour the darkness knob never reached), the image held (centred identical, stereo distinct), channels balanced + silence, faults forward atomic (BadCoeff/BadGain both channels dry, DurationTooLong, BadRange). ALES191 stereo preset, ALES41 shelf, and ALES204 mono shelf all re-run GREEN beside it; TAME bans clean. The tone axis now stands whole for mono and stereo in both plain-darkness and full-shelf forms.
loom witness=ales_stereo_reverb_shelf_witness selftest=GREEN laws=7 channels=2 max_clip=4096 bench_samples=1024 coeff=1/4 bass=2/1 treble=1/2
file active-designing/20260815-112822_fill-ales205-lotus-stereo-reverb-shelf.md the self-approved design round naming the crux, shape, and seven laws
file lotus/stereo_reverb_shelf.rye the rung — the stereo two-band reverb EQ, ALES41 shelf per ear over ALES191 wet, the shelf prechecked before the wet is written
file tools/ales_stereo_reverb_shelf_witness.rish the witness proving seven laws and re-proving ALES191/ALES41/ALES204 green beside it
recommend keep-going — the tone axis is whole for mono and stereo in both plain-darkness and full-shelf forms; the next crux is a fresh reverb axis — width (the stereo spread of the tail), freeze (an infinite-hold sustain), or early/late balance (first reflections vs the diffuse wash).
